UPDATE companies SET description='Keach & Company Woodworking operates from Chester, Virginia, where owner Karl Keach has been accepting custom commissions since 2018. Keach’s background in woodworking traces back to his father, a high school shop teacher who passed along the craft; Karl has been building projects for family and friends for most of his life before turning the work into a business. The company serves clients both locally — providing in-person service across eastern Virginia — and nationally through its website and Etsy shop.

The shop produces custom wood pieces and laser-engraved items, including challenge-coin displays (in 12-, 26-, and 50-coin configurations), commemorative plaques for organizations such as the National Park Service, serving trays and charcuterie boards in maple and walnut, custom clocks, and furniture. All pieces are milled from solid hardwoods — primarily red oak, maple, and walnut — and finished to highlight natural grain. Laser engraving is offered on wood, gold-colored, and black surfaces, allowing for badges, logos, and personalized text.

Customers span law-enforcement agencies, military units, park-ranger services, fire departments, veterans’ groups, and individual collectors. Concrete examples include a National Park Service Buffalo Badge plaque, a Chesterfield County Police badge engraving, and retirement displays for first responders. The business also creates personalized gifts for promotions, retirements, and service milestones.

Keach emphasizes a consultative approach, offering complimentary design consultations to translate each client’s vision into a finished piece. The focus on handcrafted solid-wood construction, customizable laser engraving, and direct communication with the maker is presented as the core distinction.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Laser engraving", "Challenge coin display fabrication", "Commemorative plaque manufacturing", "Serving tray production", "Charcuterie board production", "Custom clock making", "Furniture making", "Personalized text engraving", "Badge and logo engraving", "Wood finishing", "Milling", "Acrylic coin cradle installation", "9mm casing coin holder integration"], "industries": ["Law enforcement", "Military", "National Park Service", "First responders", "Fire service", "Veterans", "Collectors", "Park rangers"], "materials": ["Red oak", "Maple", "Walnut", "Acrylic", "9mm brass casings"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted from solid red oak, maple, and walnut", "Custom laser engraving on wood, gold, or black surfaces", "Complimentary design consultation for every project", "Serves law enforcement, military, first responders, and collectors", "In-person service in eastern Virginia plus nationwide online sales"], "facts_used": ["Located in Chester, Virginia -> db", "Owner Karl Keach -> /about", "Started customer projects in 2018 -> /about", "Custom woodworking and laser engraving -> /, /services", "Products: challenge coin displays, plaques, serving trays, charcuterie boards, clocks -> /", "Materials: red oak, maple, walnut, acrylic -> /", "Laser engraving on wood, gold, black -> /", "Serves law enforcement, military, park rangers, first responders, collectors -> /", "Offers complimentary consultation -> /services", "In-person services in eastern Virginia, online via website and Etsy -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "I am the owner and woodworker at Keach & Company Woodworking. I have been building projects for my family, friends, and customers since 2018.", "founded_year": "2018", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='keach-company-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kelley Bean Co. traces its roots to 1927 when the Chester B. Brown Company was founded in Morrill, Nebraska, with Robert L. Kelley Sr. as plant manager. In 1969, Robert L. Kelley Sr. and his son Gary L. Kelley established Kelley Bean Co. in Henry, Nebraska.

The company originates, processes, and markets dry edible beans — including Pinto, Great Northern, and numerous other varieties — sourced from a network of grower partnerships across the High Plains. Processing facilities run a "triple clean" line: screen sizing, gravity separation (including de-stoners), and optical electric-eye sorting, supplemented by rare-earth magnets, metal detection, and pre-wash equipment. Kelley Bean operates multiple GFSI-certified plants and maintains its own P.A.S.S. (Process Assuring Safety and Specification) food-safety system. Through a series of acquisitions — including ConAgra''s dry-bean operations in 2006 and recent purchases in North Dakota and Minnesota — the company has become one of the largest U.S. originators and processors of dry beans.

The company works directly with growers (farmers) to secure supply, and its products serve the canning, packaging, and pre-wash segments for retail and restaurant use.

Kelley Bean emphasizes absolute integrity, hard work, and community involvement as core values. Its differentiators include the internally developed P.A.S.S. system, full supply-chain control, risk-management programs, and a "grown in the USA" commitment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Dry bean origination and procurement", "Dry bean processing (cleaning, milling, sorting)", "Triple cleaning (screen sizing, gravity separation, electric eye sorting)", "Optical sorting (electric eye sorters)", "Gravity separation (de-stoners)", "Metal detection", "Rare earth magnet separation", "Pre-wash processing", "Retail and bulk packaging (Cello-Pak)", "Food safety and quality management (P.A.S.S. System)", "GFSI-certified facility operations", "AIB audit compliance", "Supply chain management", "Risk management", "Customer service and sales support"], "industries": ["Dry edible bean processing", "Food manufacturing", "Food service", "Retail food packaging", "Agriculture (grower partnerships)", "International food export"], "materials": ["Pinto beans", "Great Northern beans", "Dry edible beans (various varieties)"], "equipment": ["Electric Eyes sorting machines (Electric Sorting Machine Company)", "Cello-Pak retail packaging machine", "Round and slot hole screens (sizing)", "Gravity tables / gravity machines", "De-stoners", "Optical electric eye sorters (front and rear cameras)", "Rare earth magnets", "Metal detectors", "Pre-wash machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Internally developed P.A.S.S. food-safety system (GFSI-aligned)", "Full supply-chain control from grower to packaged product", "\"Triple clean\" processing line with optical sorting, gravity separation, and metal detection", "Employee- and family-owned structure with multi-generational leadership", "GFSI-certified facilities and annual AIB audits"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1927 as Chester B. Brown Co. -> /about", "Kelley Bean Co. founded 1969 by Robert L. Kelley Sr. and Gary L. Kelley -> /about", "Headquartered in Scottsbluff, Nebraska -> /, /about", "Employee- and family-owned -> /, /about", "Fourth generation led by Kevin Kelley -> /about", "One of the largest originators and processors of dry beans in the U.S. -> /, /about", "Triple clean processing: screen sizing, gravity separation, electric eye sorting -> /quality", "Equipment: Electric Eyes, Cello-Pak, gravity machines, de-stoners, optical sorters, rare earth magnets, metal detectors, pre-wash machines -> /quality", "P.A.S.S. System (Process Assuring Safety and Specification) internally developed, GFSI-aligned -> /quality", "Multiple GFSI-certified facilities and annual AIB audits -> /quality", "Acquisitions: ConAgra dry bean ops (2006), Yellowstone Bean (2015), Cavalier Bean (2019), Ottertail Bean (2024), Green Valley Bean (2026) -> /about", "Serves growers, customers (food manufacturers, food service, retail), consumers -> /", "Products: Pinto, Great Northern, and every variety in between -> /", "Values: integrity, hard work, dedication, service, community involvement -> /", "Differentiators: customer service, supply chain control, food quality & safety, grown in USA, industry experience, risk management -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "processes and sells the dry edible beans which are sourced directly from its local community of grower partnerships", "founded_year": "1927", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kelley-bean-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='KeyStone Co-Pack Manufacturing, LLC is based in Pleasant Grove, Utah. The company does not publish its founding date or ownership details, but it presents itself as a turnkey co-pack partner for supplement and personal-care brands.

The firm provides end-to-end contract manufacturing for nutritional and cosmetic products. Its service chain covers ideation, formulation development, raw-material sourcing, production, packaging, and fulfillment. Production capabilities include powder blending and filling, capsule and tablet manufacturing, and packaging in jars, gusseted bags, bottles, sticks, sachets, tubs, and vials. The company notes a large inventory of hundreds of ingredients and custom formulas, but does not disclose facility size, headcount, or annual volume.

KeyStone serves three primary industry groups: Food & Beverage (protein powders, baking mixes, unpasteurized beverage shots), Health & Wellness (protein blends, electrolytes, pre-workouts, performance and wellness powdered supplements), and Personal Care & Beauty (hair care, skin care, oral care products).

The company emphasizes its turnkey model as a differentiator, citing cost efficiency, access to a wider supplier network, regulatory knowledge, and specialized expertise. It also highlights responsible sourcing practices and nearby fulfillment partners to shorten delivery times.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ideation and concept development", "Formulation development", "Raw material sourcing", "Powder blending and filling", "Capsule manufacturing", "Tablet manufacturing", "Jar filling", "Gusseted bag filling", "Stick pack packaging", "Sachet packaging", "Tub filling", "Bottle filling", "Vial filling", "Labeling and sealing", "Order fulfillment and delivery"], "industries": ["Food & Beverage", "Health & Wellness", "Personal Care & Beauty"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full turnkey service from ideation through fulfillment", "R&D team with access to hundreds of ingredients and custom formulas", "Responsible sourcing with compliance to industry standards", "Multiple packaging formats including capsules, sticks, sachets, and vials", "Local fulfillment partners for faster shipping"], "facts_used": ["Location: Pleasant Grove, Utah -> db", "Turnkey services: ideation, formulation, sourcing, production, packaging, delivery -> /", "Production capabilities: powder blend/fill, capsules, tablets, jars, gusseted bags -> /", "Packaging formats: capsules, tablets, sticks, sachets, tubs, gusseted bags, bottles, jars, vials -> /", "Industries served: Food & Beverage, Health & Wellness, Personal Care & Beauty -> /", "Product examples: protein powders, baking mixes, unpasteurized beverages, protein blends, electrolytes, pre-workouts, hair care, skincare, oral care -> /", "R&D scientists and large inventory of hundreds of ingredients -> /", "Responsible sourcing and compliance with industry standards -> /", "Fulfillment partners nearby -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / jo