UPDATE companies SET description='Keystone Solutions Group operates from Kalamazoo, Michigan, where it has provided medical device contract manufacturing services for more than 25 years. The company is led by President Jim Medsker and a leadership team that includes VP of Sales and Business Development Jason Barr, VP of Engineering Vaughn Gerber, and Director of Quality & Regulatory William Reinholt.

The company specializes in assembly, kitting, packaging, converting, and sterilization management, supporting programs from prototype and pilot builds through full-scale production. Its facility includes multiple clean room environments, and it extends beyond core manufacturing to offer supply chain sourcing, warehousing, and distribution services. A dedicated Customer Product Transfer Process manages product transfers from project planning to commercial release.

Keystone serves the medical device industry worldwide, producing single-use disposable and reusable medical products. Its customers range from start-ups to established OEMs seeking end-to-end manufacturing, packaging, and sterilization solutions.

The company emphasizes a collaborative approach that addresses regulatory, intellectual property, and commercial challenges, aiming to break the mold of typical OEM/contract manufacturer relationships. Its stated values focus on complete end-to-end solutions from concept through approval and production.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Assembly", "Kitting", "Packaging", "Converting", "Sterilization management", "Clean room manufacturing", "Supply chain sourcing", "Warehousing", "Distribution", "Product transfer management", "Testing", "Regulatory compliance support", "Intellectual property management"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Medical device contract manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototypes to full-scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complete end-to-end solutions from concept through approval and production", "Collaborative approach addressing regulatory, IP, and commercial challenges", "Multiple clean room environments for sterile manufacturing", "Supply chain sourcing, warehousing, and distribution integrated with manufacturing", "Customer Product Transfer Process managing transfers from planning to commercial release"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Kalamazoo, Michigan -> /about", "In operation for more than 25 years -> /about", "President Jim Medsker, VP Sales Jason Barr, VP Engineering Vaughn Gerber, Director Quality William Reinholt -> /about", "Services: assembly, kitting, packaging, converting, sterilization management -> / and /about", "Prototype to full-scale production -> / and /about", "Multiple clean room environments -> / and /about", "Supply chain sourcing, warehousing, distribution -> / and /about", "Customer Product Transfer Process -> / and /about", "Medical device industry, single-use disposable and reusable products -> /about", "Collaborative approach addressing regulatory, IP, commercial challenges -> /about", "End-to-end solutions from concept through approval and production -> /about", "Team members listed (Amy Pequeno, April Stickels, etc.) -> /about", "ISO 13485, QSR, GMP mentioned in job context -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Keystone specializes in assembly, kitting, packaging, converting and sterilization management from prototypes and pilot builds to full-scale production.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='keystone-solutions-group' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kifaru International operates from Riverton, Wyoming, where it designs and sells a line of hunting packs, technical apparel, duffels, and shelter systems. The company emphasizes an "American Made" positioning and collaborates with camouflage brands such as Mossy Oak and MultiCam. A founding year, ownership structure, or founder names are not disclosed in public sources.

The product range centers on backcountry hunting gear: frame packs (Stryker XL, Hellbender, 44 Mag, 357 Mag, Kutthroat, Bedlam, The Maniml), bino harnesses, hip quivers, and pocket organizers; merino and synthetic apparel including base layers, fleece, insulated jackets, and softshell pants; duffels (Blitz Bag, Rampart, Kenosha, Rondy); plus game bags, shelters, and gun bearers. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are published.

The brand targets serious big-game hunters — elk, moose, caribou, and bear — as evidenced by its film series documenting hunts in Alaska, Colorado, Utah, and British Columbia.

Kifaru differentiates itself through domestic manufacturing claims and limited-edition camouflage partnerships, notably the Mossy Oak Fall Foliage and Treestand patterns. The company also produces a media arm, Kifaru Films, which publishes hunt documentaries on YouTube to build community around the gear.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hunting pack design and manufacturing", "Technical apparel manufacturing", "Duffel bag manufacturing", "Shelter manufacturing", "Accessory manufacturing", "Product design", "Direct-to-consumer sales", "Media content production"], "industries": ["Hunting", "Outdoor recreation", "Backcountry hunting", "Big-game hunting"], "materials": ["Merino wool", "Synthetic insulation", "Grid fleece", "Softshell fabric", "Mossy Oak camouflage fabric", "MultiCam camouflage fabric"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["\"American Made\" manufacturing claim", "Limited-edition Mossy Oak camouflage collaborations", "Direct-to-consumer e-commerce with hunt-film media arm (Kifaru Films)", "Product line focused on backcountry big-game hunting"], "facts_used": ["Company name: Kifaru International -> db", "Headquarters: Riverton, Wyoming -> db", "Website: kifaru.net -> db", "Product categories: hunting packs, apparel, duffels, shelters, accessories -> /", "\"American Made\" claim -> /", "Mossy Oak camouflage partnership -> /", "MultiCam camouflage offered -> /", "Kifaru Films YouTube channel -> /", "Hunt films featuring elk, moose, caribou, bear hunts in Alaska, Colorado, Utah, BC -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "\"Premier Hunting Gear & Accessories | Kifaru \u2013 Kifaru Intl\" and \"American Made meets America''s Camouflage\" with branded product listings (Stryker XL, Hellbender, Blitz Bag, etc.) at set prices", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kifaru-international' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kiliper Corporation operates from Ames, Iowa, where it has produced packaging solutions for more than 25 years. The business was built on a family-owned foundation and now operates as part of Inovar Packaging Group, a national packaging partner that provides expanded resources and a broader manufacturing network while maintaining Kiliper''s responsive, service-driven approach.

The company specializes in stretch sleeve labeling, roll-fed label technologies, and flexible packaging solutions, supported by advanced flexographic printing capabilities and deep material expertise. Its offerings include printed and laminated film solutions, sustainable and recyclable packaging options, and prepress services. Kiliper also runs an innovation lab at Inovar headquarters for research and development and provides vendor-managed inventory programs to streamline supply chains.

Kiliper serves brands across food and beverage, personal and home care, industrial, pet care, agricultural chemical, supplements and nutraceuticals, household products, and agriculture markets. Its stretch sleeves conform to container shapes using material elasticity, eliminating heat or adhesives, while roll-fed labels are designed for high-speed application and seamless container coverage.

The company emphasizes quick turnaround times, adaptable production capabilities, and a hands-on, customer-first team focused on long-term partnerships. Its differentiators include specialized expertise in stretch sleeve and roll-fed label applications, reliable processes that ensure consistent quality, and scalable support through Inovar''s nationwide network.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Stretch sleeve labeling", "Roll-fed label production", "Flexible packaging solutions", "Flexographic printing", "Prepress services", "Vendor managed inventory (VMI) programs", "Innovation lab / R&D", "Sustainable packaging options", "Recyclable packaging options", "Printed and laminated film solutions"], "industries": ["Food & beverage", "Personal & home care", "Industrial", "Pet care", "Ag chemical", "Supplements & nutraceuticals", "Household products", "Agriculture"], "materials": ["Printed and laminated films", "Sustainable materials", "Recyclable materials", "Lightweight film constructions"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quick turnaround times and adaptable production capabilities for a wide range of program scales", "Hands-on, service-driven team focused on building long-term relationships", "Deep knowledge of stretch sleeve and roll-fed label applications across industries", "Reliable processes and proven capabilities ensuring consistent quality", "Backed by Inovar''s nationwide network offering expanded resources and production flexibility"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Ames, Iowa -> db", "Family-owned foundation -> /about-us", "Part of Inovar Packaging Group -> / and /about-us", "Over 25 years in business -> / and /about-us", "Specializes in stretch sleeve labeling, roll-fed labels, flexible packaging -> / and /about-us", "Advanced flexographic printing capabilities -> /about-us", "Prepress services -> /", "Vendor managed inventory programs -> /", "Innovation lab at Inovar headquarters -> /", "Sustainable and recyclable packaging options -> /", "Printed and laminated film solutions -> /", "Industries: food & beverage, personal & home care, industrial, pet care, ag chemical, supplements & nutraceuticals, household products, agriculture -> / and /about-us", "Stretch sleeves use material elasticity, no heat/adhesives -> /", "Roll-fed labels for high-speed application -> /", "Quick turnaround times, adaptable production -> / and /about-us", "Customer-first approach, long-term partnerships -> /about-us", "Scalable support through Inovar nationwide network -> / and /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kiliper specializes in stretch sleeve and roll-fed label technologies, supported by flexible packaging solutions that deliver performance, efficiency, and strong visual presence. With advanced flexographic printing capabilities and deep material expertise, Kiliper produces consistent results across a wide range of packaging applications.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kiliper-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Killian''s Custom Metal Roofing & Panel LLC operates from Des Moines, Iowa, where it was founded in the fall of 2013 by Paula Killian. The venture traces back to the late 1990s when Killian worked at a steel company in Tulsa, Oklahoma, selling coil to roll-former operators. After visiting manufacturing plants, she sought hands-on experience and joined B&M Metals in Murrayville, Georgia, under Chris Bryan, learning panel fabrication and trim production before launching her own operation.

The company manufactures custom-cut, three-foot-wide metal roof panels and matching trim. Its core product line includes Tuff Rib panels rolled from 29-gauge steel with a Sherwin-Williams WeatherX finish that carries a 40-year warranty, available in 22 colors or a Galvalume substrate. It also fabricates standing-seam profiles and distributes commercial architectural systems such as R-Panel, PBR, corrugated, and other wall and roof profiles. In-house capabilities cover panel roll-forming, trim fabrication, and full installation services.

Customers span residential homeowners, agricultural builders erecting pole barns, and commercial contractors specifying architectural wall and roof systems. The firm supplies both direct-to-owner projects and trade accounts needing repair or replacement panels matched to existing profiles.

