UPDATE companies SET description='LC Fine Foods, operating as LC Cash and Carry, has been a fixture in New Haven, Connecticut since 1965. The company was founded by Italian immigrant Italo "Leo" Ciocca, who envisioned bringing the finest Italian imports to his community. What began as a modest enterprise grew into a family-owned wholesale and retail food business that continues under the leadership of Ciocca''s children, Carlo and Danny.

The company distributes a broad assortment of Italian and domestic food products across categories that include produce, deli meats, cheeses, pasta, olive oils, bakery goods, coffee, and seasonal specialties.

Its customer base spans restaurants, delicatessens, institutional kitchens, and individual consumers. A deli operator in New Haven County cites the company as a primary supplier for fresh produce and cold cuts, while retail shoppers seek out traditional items such as panettone and pandoro during the holidays.

