UPDATE companies SET description='LGC Maine Standards operates from Cumberland Foreside, Maine. The business originated as Maine Standards Company, LLC, a specialist in linearity and calibration verification with more than a century of experience in that niche. In November 2015, the company was acquired by LGC, a global life sciences measurement and testing firm founded in 1842 and now owned by funds affiliated with KKR. The acquisition brought Maine Standards into LGC’s portfolio of reference materials, proficiency testing, and genomics reagents.

At its Maine facility, the company manufactures liquid, ready-to-use, multi-level calibration verification sets under the VALIDATE® brand, designed for the most widely used clinical laboratory instruments. The modern laboratory and streamlined processes support production of these quality-control products, which are shipped on customer schedules.

The products serve clinical laboratories and healthcare professionals across diagnostics, pharmaceuticals, agricultural biotechnology, food safety, environmental testing, government agencies, and academic research. LGC’s broader measurement services also underpin safety and regulatory compliance in these sectors.

