UPDATE companies SET description='LIW Furniture operates as Lancaster Iron & Wood, a family-owned custom furniture and cabinetry company rooted in Lancaster County, Pennsylvania. The business is owned by Case Taylor, who brought hands-on experience from Amish Artisan Woodcraft in cabinetry, millwork, and custom furniture to the operation. The company describes its shop as a Lancaster, PA wood shop where all pieces are hand crafted, though its website also lists a Navarre, Ohio address.

The company produces custom hardwood and iron furniture including dining tables, chairs, cabinets, built-ins, vanities, bars, and office furniture. Its team works with locally sourced hardwoods from native Appalachian forests, many from Pennsylvania, and offers live-edge tops, custom base options, a range of stains and paints, and proprietary hardware and metal features. Customers can select from a catalogue of solid-wood designs or collaborate with designers and craftsmen on fully custom pieces for residential or commercial projects.

LIW serves homeowners, restaurants, retail spaces, offices, and other commercial clients. A restaurant owner, John Harris, noted the company produced dining tables for his establishment, while residential customers Sarah Benhayon and Jacqueline Swazy referenced custom dining sets and live-edge tables. The firm emphasizes its ability to handle projects small and large, from a single dining set to a full restaurant fit-out.

Taylor states the goal is to continue building on the craftsmanship LIW has long been known for while expanding custom possibilities. The company highlights its control over materials through local partnerships, a quality standard that every piece must be acceptable in their own homes, and a professional team of designers, project managers, and craftsmen who bring pride and passion to each project.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture manufacturing", "Cabinetry and millwork", "Live-edge table fabrication", "Custom base design and fabrication", "Wood finishing (stains, paints, combinations)", "Metal hardware and feature fabrication", "Custom cabinetry, built-ins, vanities, bars", "Office furniture manufacturing", "Commercial-grade furniture production", "Residential furniture manufacturing"], "industries": ["Residential", "Hospitality (restaurants)", "Retail", "Commercial office"], "materials": ["Appalachian hardwoods", "Pennsylvania native hardwoods", "Iron"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Locally sourced Appalachian hardwoods from Pennsylvania forests", "Hand crafted in Lancaster, PA wood shop", "Custom design collaboration with in-house craftsmen", "Live-edge table tops and custom base options", "Proprietary hardware and metal features unique to the shop"], "facts_used": ["Family-owned, Case Taylor owner -> /about", "Located in Lancaster County, PA; hand crafted in Lancaster wood shop -> /", "Background in Amish Artisan Woodcraft -> /about", "Products: hardwood/iron tables, chairs, cabinets, built-ins, vanities, bars, office furniture -> /about, /", "Materials: locally sourced Appalachian hardwoods, Pennsylvania native -> /", "Custom design with craftsmen, live edge, custom bases, finishes, hardware -> /", "Industries: homes, restaurants, retail, offices, commercial -> /about", "Testimonials: restaurant dining tables, residential dining sets -> /about", "Quality standard: acceptable in own homes -> /", "Team: designers, project managers, craftsmen -> /about", "Address on site: Navarre, OH -> /, /about", "Database HQ: East Earl, PA -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All pieces are hand crafted in our Lancaster, Pa wood shop.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='liw-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LQ Mechatronics operates from Branford, Connecticut, as the U.S. arm of the LQ Group, a German system supplier specializing in electromechanical complete solutions for machine and plant engineering.

The company designs and manufactures modular control cabinets, energy guide systems, and custom cable assemblies, all built around its EnergyLink system kit—a standardized set of connectors, power cables, distributors, and functional modules that eliminate interface issues. It also assembles drag chains (energy chains) and provides end-to-end services from engineering through logistics. The group reports 365 specialists across three locations, producing 305,000 systems and 2,990 kilometers of cable annually.

LQ Mechatronics serves machine builders, plant constructors, and the packaging industry, evidenced by its membership in the Packaging Valley network since 2016. Its solutions are used in automation environments requiring robust, pre-assembled energy chains and compact functional modules such as the A-TEC series.

