UPDATE companies SET description='Laguna Fabrics was founded in 1986 in Los Angeles, California, by Monet Goode and has been operated by the Roshan family across multiple generations. The company began as a circular knitting mill serving the contemporary fashion market and has remained a family-owned business for nearly 35 years.

The mill runs in-house circular knitting machines from low to fine gauge, with a capacity of 1.5 million pounds per month, and offers special finishes such as brushing and sueding along with fabric laundering. Services include technical fabric analysis, new construction engineering, on-trend fabric development, on-demand sample yardage, and a showroom with a complete lab-dip catalog.

Laguna supplies trend-forward knits to contemporary fashion brands, independent designers, and start-up labels, emphasizing quick turnaround enabled by domestic production.

The company’s differentiation rests on its GOTS certification—it claims to be the only circular knit mill in the United States with that credential—and a commitment to provenance, process transparency, and product authenticity. Since 2000 it has shifted toward lower-impact materials, joining the Textile Exchange and the California Cotton & Climate Coalition, with a stated goal of reaching 90 percent sustainable material output by 2025.', certifications=ARRAY['GOTS','GRS','SGS Eco Product Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Circular knitting (low to fine gauge)", "Brushing and sueding finishes", "Fabric laundering", "Technical fabric analysis", "New construction engineering", "On-trend fabric development", "On-demand sample yardage", "In-person showroom appointments", "Lab-dip catalog for color reference", "Multi-layer quality control protocol", "Yarn inventory: GOTS organic cotton, TENCEL\u2122 lyocell, TENCEL\u2122 modal, recycled cotton, hemp"], "industries": ["Fashion", "Apparel", "Textile", "Designer brands", "Start-ups", "Sustainable textiles"], "materials": ["GOTS Organic Cotton", "TENCEL\u2122 Lyocell", "TENCEL\u2122 Modal", "Recycled Cotton", "Hemp", "Climate Beneficial\u2122 Cotton"], "equipment": ["Circular knitting machines (low to fine gauge)"], "volume": "1.5 million pounds per month knitting capacity", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only circular knit mill in the U.S. with GOTS certification", "In-house circular knitting with 1.5 million pounds per month capacity", "Domestic manufacturing in Los Angeles for quick turnaround", "Focus on certified sustainable fibers (GOTS organic cotton, TENCEL\u2122, recycled cotton, hemp)", "Family-owned since 1986 with multi-generational expertise"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 in Los Angeles, California -> /about", "Family-owned, operated by Roshan family -> /about", "Founder Monet Goode -> /about", "40 employees -> db, /about", "In-house circular knitting machines low to fine gauge -> /about", "1.5 million pounds per month knitting capacity -> /about", "Special finishes: brushing and sueding -> /about", "Fabric laundering capacity -> /about", "10+ million yards produced to date -> /about", "Certified sustainable fibers: GOTS organic cotton, TENCEL\u2122 lyocell, TENCEL\u2122 modal, recycled cotton, hemp -> /about", "GOTS certified, only circular knit mill in USA with GOTS -> /about", "GRS certified recycled cotton -> /about", "SGS Eco Product Certified -> db/products", "Services: technical fabric analysis, new construction engineering, on-trend fabric development, on-demand sample yardage, showroom, lab-dip catalog -> /about", "Customers: contemporary fashion brands, young designers, smaller start-ups -> /about, /", "Quick turnaround due to domestic manufacturing -> /, /about", "Joined Textile Exchange 2018 -> /about", "Joined California Cotton & Climate Coalition (C4) 2021 -> /about", "Goal 90% sustainable material output by 2025 -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We proudly manufacture all fabrics in our knitting mill in Los Angeles, California", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "40", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='laguna-fabrics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lakeland Engineering Equipment Company, headquartered in Kansas City, Kansas, traces its roots to 1952 when Bill Fox founded the business in Minneapolis as a family-owned distributor of process motor controls and electrical components. Over seven decades, the company has grown from a Midwestern supplier into an international enterprise with locations across four states.

The company operates as a broad-line distributor for more than 100 electrical component manufacturers, stocking items such as motor controls, solenoid valves, drives, switches, PLCs, HMIs, and explosion-proof components. Beyond distribution, Lakeland provides equipment rentals for power monitoring and quality testing, engineering and consulting services, custom electrical enclosure fabrication through its Delta Fabricating division, and inventory management programs designed to prevent supply-chain disruptions.

Lakeland serves industrial and commercial customers that rely on electrical control systems, process automation, and hazardous-location equipment. Its client base includes organizations needing rapid access to replacement parts, custom enclosure solutions, and on-site technical support for critical infrastructure.

The company''s stated differentiator is a refusal to force customers to choose among quality components, expert service, and fast delivery—a commitment articulated since its founding and reinforced through decades of expansion.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical component distribution", "Equipment rental (power monitoring, quality testing)", "Engineering and consulting services", "Custom electrical enclosure design and fabrication", "Inventory management and stocking programs"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Approved distributor for over 100 leading electrical component manufacturers", "Equipment rentals for power monitoring and quality testing", "Custom electrical enclosure design and fabrication (Delta Fabricating)", "Inventory management programs to prevent supply-chain disruptions", "Engineering expertise with decades of experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1952 by Bill Fox in Minneapolis -> /about", "Family-owned Midwest distributor -> /about", "Headquartered in Kansas City, Kansas -> db", "Distributes electrical motor controls and components from over 100 manufacturers -> /", "Offers equipment rentals for power monitoring and quality testing -> /", "Provides engineering services and custom electrical enclosures via Delta Fabricating -> /", "Operates locations in four states (Minneapolis, Kansas, Omaha, Denver) -> /about", "Commitment to quality components, excellent service, and fast delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Lakeland Engineering Equipment Company distributes top-quality electrical motor controls and components.", "founded_year": "1952", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lakeland-engineering-equipment-company-kansas-city' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lakeside Steel & Mfg. Co. operates from Kenosha, Wisconsin, where it has served the metal fabrication needs of the power generation industry, material handling, construction equipment, and original equipment manufacturers for over 100 years. The company’s history spans more than a century, though a specific founding year is not publicly stated.

The 41,000-square-foot facility houses a range of in-house processes including plasma and flame cutting, sawing, bending, rolling, punching, certified welding, and painting. A 600-ton hydraulic press brake, four plate rolls, twenty-two welding machines, and multiple overhead cranes support heavy fabrication; the shop has produced weldments as large as 13 feet 6 inches in diameter by 70 feet long weighing over 105,000 pounds. An adjacent 11,000-square-foot warehouse stocks carbon and stainless steel sheet, plate, and structural shapes, enabling rapid material availability. For specialized requirements, Lakeside coordinates stress relieving, blast cleaning, galvanizing, machining, and non-destructive testing through qualified subcontractors.

Customers span power generation, material handling, construction equipment, and OEM sectors. Project examples include combustors, air piping, coal ducts, trommels, inlet water pipes, forklift booms, shaker conveyors, fly ash silos, cement hoppers, explosion-door components, galvanized platforms, and a variety of structural frames and enclosures.

Lakeside emphasizes short lead times through multi-shift operations and an on-site steel inventory that eliminates delivery delays. Its location midway between Chicago and Milwaukee provides direct highway and rail access for nationwide shipping. The company cites its certified craftsmen, heavy-lifting capacity, and commitment to precise, timely fabrication as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plasma cutting", "Flame cutting", "Sawing (bandsaw)", "Bending (press brake)", "Plate rolling", "Punching (ironworker)", "Certified welding (MIG/TIG/stick)", "Painting (electrostatic and airless)", "Stress relieving (subcontracted)", "Blast cleaning (subcontracted)", "Galvanizing (subcontracted)", "Machining (subcontracted)", "Non-destructive testing (subcontracted)", "Beveling (rotary mechanical, nibbler, oxy-fuel)", "Shearing", "Ironworking (angle cutting/punching)", "Material handling (overhead cranes, jib cranes, forklifts)", "Local delivery (stake trucks, pickup)", "Large fabrication (up to 105,000 lbs)", "CNC plasma/oxy-fuel cutting", "Press brake forming (600 ton)", "Turning rolls (up to 60 tons)", "Machining (radial drill, lathe, mill, tapping, threading)", "Steel inventory management"], "industries": ["Power Generation", "Material Handling", "Construction Equipment", "Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEM)"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Sheet", "Plate", "Structural shapes"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma/flame cutting machine (8\" thick, 11'' x 42'' water table)", "600-ton hydraulic press brake (5/8\" x 12'')", "Four plate rolls (1\" thick x 12'')", "Twenty-two welding machines (300-650 amp)", "Five overhead cranes (5-20 ton)", "Eight jib cranes (1-2 ton)", "Outside overhead crane (10 ton)", "5,000 lb forklift", "Three bandsaws (20\" x 25\" auto feed)", "Two shears (5/8\" x 12'')", "Two ironworkers (6\" x 6\" x 1/2\")", "Three beveling systems (Gullco rotary mechanical beveller, Heck portable nibbler,