UPDATE companies SET description='Levison Enterprises operates from a 15,000-square-foot facility in Millbury, Ohio, where it has been based since 2014. The company began as an AC plasma display manufacturer with in-house electronic manufacturing capabilities. As printed circuit board technology advanced and demand for plasma displays waned, the engineering team pivoted to become a full-service electronic contract manufacturer and sub-assembly provider. The business is organized as a limited liability company led by President David M. Levison.

The company provides turnkey electronic manufacturing services including printed circuit board assembly, cable and wire harness fabrication, electronic repair and diagnostics, PCB design and engineering, rapid prototyping, and legacy product repair with reverse engineering. Its facility features ESD-safe epoxy flooring, semi-truck access, and on-site engineering and supply chain management. Levison holds AS9100, ISO 9001, and ISO 13485 certifications through NSF-ISR, is ITAR registered, and complies with IPC and J-STD standards while working toward CMMC compliance.

Levison serves military and aerospace, medical device, food safety, industrial, and defense customers. Case studies reference Seagate Mobile Security Solutions for security systems, EPI Global for legacy displays dating to the 1960s, and international clients who value faster shipping and engineering responsiveness. The company also supports design engineers who need a manufacturing partner for prototype through production runs.

Levison emphasizes a culture of continuous improvement, targeting 100% quality, on-time delivery, and customer satisfaction. Its differentiators include a vetted domestic supply chain with counterfeit-part mitigation, on-site engineers for real-time problem solving, PFMEA-driven process controls, and a single-project-manager model for turnkey programs.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ITAR registered','CMMC (in process)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed circuit board assembly (through-hole and surface mount)", "Cable and wire harness assembly", "Electronic repair and diagnostics", "PCB design and layout engineering", "Rapid prototyping", "Medical device manufacturing (ISO 13485)", "Legacy product repair and reverse engineering", "Retrofitting and upgrades", "Supply chain management and logistics", "Counterfeit parts mitigation", "Process Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (PFMEA)", "On-site engineering support", "Sensor and firmware development", "Turnkey design-to-build and build-to-print manufacturing", "ITAR-compliant manufacturing", "CMMC compliance readiness", "AS9100/ISO 9001/ISO 13485 quality management systems", "ESD-controlled manufacturing environment"], "industries": ["Military and aerospace", "Medical devices", "Food safety", "Industrial and defense", "Government"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AS9100, ISO 9001, ISO 13485 certified by NSF-ISR", "ITAR registered with IPC/J-STD compliance", "15,000 sq ft ESD-safe domestic facility", "Turnkey design-to-build and build-to-print with on-site engineering", "Legacy product repair and reverse engineering without original documentation"], "facts_used": ["Location: Millbury, Ohio -> /about", "Facility: 15,000 sq ft built 2014 -> /about", "History: started as AC plasma display manufacturer -> /about", "Leadership: David M. Levison, President -> /about", "Certifications: AS9100, ISO 9001, ISO 13485 by NSF-ISR, ITAR registered, IPC/J-STD, CMMC -> / and /about", "Capabilities: electronic assembly, cable/harness, repair, PCB design, rapid prototyping, medical device, legacy repair, reverse engineering -> / and /capabilities", "Industries: military/aerospace, medical, food safety, industrial/defense -> / and /capabilities", "Case studies: Seagate Mobile Security Solutions, EPI Global -> /", "Quality focus: 100% quality, on-time delivery, customer satisfaction -> /about", "Turnkey model with single project manager -> /capabilities", "Vetted supply chain, counterfeit mitigation -> /capabilities", "On-site engineering, PFMEA -> /capabilities", "ESD-safe facility, semi-truck accessible -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Levison Enterprises LLC is a full-service design to build and build to print manufacturer that takes your ideas or designs and can turn them into a finished quality built product.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='levison-enterprises' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Leviton, headquartered in Melville, New York, was founded in 1906. Over more than a century, the company has grown into a manufacturer of electrical wiring devices, lighting controls, data networking infrastructure, and energy management solutions.

The product portfolio spans switches, dimmers, outlets, and lighting controls for residential and commercial use; TrueArc AFCI breakers designed to reduce nuisance tripping; fusion splicing solutions for fiber optic installations; the My Leviton app for unified smart home control of lighting, load management, and EV charging; Series 2500 utility submeters with tool-free connectors; Leviton Load Centers for modern electrical panels; data center cabling and infrastructure; Arc-Arrest switch-rated pin and sleeve devices; and dockside power accessories. Recent investments include a $100 million global capital expansion for AI and smart building network infrastructure.

Leviton serves residential homeowners, electrical contractors, data center operators, utility companies, and marine dock operators. Its solutions appear in new home construction, commercial buildings, high-density data centers, utility submetering programs, and shore power installations.

